WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:01.611
- I just always knew.

00:00:01.611 --> 00:00:03.994
I just always knew, one day,
that I'm going to be doing this.

00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:05.013
I knew.

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:07.930
And, eventually, I just went
up to one of the managers,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.573
and I was like, "I have
to have this song."

00:00:10.573 --> 00:00:13.726
Doing what you want means moving forward

00:00:13.726 --> 00:00:15.066
with the way you feel.

00:00:15.066 --> 00:00:16.848
I'm 21, so I'm going to live my life

00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:18.628
like I'm a 21-year-old.

00:00:18.628 --> 00:00:21.007
I'm going to dress like I'm a 21-year-old.

00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:23.505
- She's a Barbadian singer and songwriter.

00:00:23.505 --> 00:00:26.314
With sales exceeding 200
million records worldwide,

00:00:26.314 --> 00:00:29.005
she's one of the best-selling
artists of all time.

00:00:29.005 --> 00:00:32.825
She has an estimated net
worth of $230 million.

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:34.496
She is Rihanna, and here is my take

00:00:34.496 --> 00:00:36.479
on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:37.979
Clip number one is my favorite,

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:39.390
and make sure to stick around all the way

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.890
till the end for some special bonus clips.

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:47.232
- I always loved music.

00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:48.732
I always loved it.

00:00:49.662 --> 00:00:51.726
Then, I would start singing along,

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:53.026
and, before you knew it,

00:00:53.026 --> 00:00:55.394
I wanted to be that person so bad

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:59.037
that I would lip sync or
dance or look in the mirror

00:00:59.037 --> 00:01:02.120
or perform for my friends or cousins,

00:01:03.975 --> 00:01:06.096
and I just always knew.

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:07.329
I just always knew, one day,

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:08.677
that I'm going to be doing this.

00:01:08.677 --> 00:01:09.872
I knew.

00:01:09.872 --> 00:01:11.712
Well, the first time I heard "Umbrella,"

00:01:11.712 --> 00:01:13.676
I just knew how much I loved the song.

00:01:13.676 --> 00:01:16.725
I thought it had one of
the most original songs

00:01:16.725 --> 00:01:19.418
of any song that I've ever heard thus far,

00:01:19.418 --> 00:01:20.338
and I just ...

00:01:20.338 --> 00:01:21.848
Especially the ones that I've recording,

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.077
and I just ...

00:01:23.077 --> 00:01:24.231
I was like, "I have to have this one.

00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:25.064
I have to have it."

00:01:25.064 --> 00:01:25.897
- But everybody wanted it, right?

00:01:25.897 --> 00:01:28.706
- Well, I didn't know that at the time.

00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:29.804
At the time, they were like,

00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:32.169
"Okay, you can have this song," whatever.

00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:33.771
I was like, "I have to have it."

00:01:33.771 --> 00:01:34.842
That's when we started finding,

00:01:34.842 --> 00:01:37.721
"Okay, hold on a second,"
'cause this person is listening,

00:01:37.721 --> 00:01:39.913
that person's listening.

00:01:39.913 --> 00:01:42.493
Eventually, I just went
up to one of the managers,

00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:43.912
and I was like,

00:01:43.912 --> 00:01:45.256
"I have to have this song.

00:01:45.256 --> 00:01:46.516
This song is mine."

00:01:46.516 --> 00:01:47.745
I basically was like,

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:49.686
"I'm going to fight you if
I don't have this song."

00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:50.878
(laughing)

00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:54.051
- How social media affects
the way that you make music?

00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:56.071
Do you consider feedback from fans?

00:01:56.071 --> 00:01:57.988
- Absolutely, big time.

00:01:59.413 --> 00:02:04.027
My fans definitely have an
impact on the way I make music,

00:02:04.027 --> 00:02:05.504
what I do.

00:02:05.504 --> 00:02:09.573
It still comes from me, and I still like

00:02:09.573 --> 00:02:12.075
to show them new things,

00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:15.158
but I always want to make sure that ...

00:02:18.539 --> 00:02:19.967
I have to pay attention.

00:02:19.967 --> 00:02:23.621
They say things that you need to hear.

00:02:23.621 --> 00:02:25.072
They're out there in the world.

00:02:25.072 --> 00:02:27.125
They're not in the little box here.

00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:28.756
They know what's going on,

00:02:28.756 --> 00:02:32.256
and you would be stupid to be so oblivious

00:02:33.722 --> 00:02:35.307
to what they're saying.

00:02:35.307 --> 00:02:36.929
You have to pay attention.

00:02:36.929 --> 00:02:40.038
Every album, for me,
has been a natural step

00:02:40.038 --> 00:02:41.489
in my growth.

00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:44.278
It has displayed that the different steps

00:02:44.278 --> 00:02:45.550
in my career,

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:49.717
and every one happens to be
better than the previous one.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.771
For me, that's the most important thing,

00:02:54.771 --> 00:02:57.514
just making sure that every
time you do something,

00:02:57.514 --> 00:03:01.595
you do it better than you did it before.

00:03:01.595 --> 00:03:04.616
Even when I listen to my
music or watch my videos,

00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:08.783
for instance, from "Pon de
Replay" to "Russian Roulette,"

00:03:09.798 --> 00:03:11.655
it's not even the same person.

00:03:11.655 --> 00:03:12.964
It's not even the same person,

00:03:12.964 --> 00:03:16.525
but I don't know anyone who
has been the same person

00:03:16.525 --> 00:03:18.775
at 17 that they were at 21.

00:03:19.837 --> 00:03:23.187
I think a lot of people
think that them doing

00:03:23.187 --> 00:03:27.354
what they want means doing what
everybody else doesn't want,

00:03:28.765 --> 00:03:30.265
and it's not that.

00:03:31.104 --> 00:03:34.255
Doing what you want means moving forward

00:03:34.255 --> 00:03:37.467
with the way you feel
and living your truth,

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.917
and, a lot of the times,

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:40.776
you'll find common ground with people,

00:03:40.776 --> 00:03:43.298
and, sometimes, there are a
lot of people you won't find

00:03:43.298 --> 00:03:46.941
that agree with you, but
it has to be your truth,

00:03:46.941 --> 00:03:49.274
because that's the only way.

00:03:52.153 --> 00:03:56.106
Well, it's definitely the
ultimate dream for me,

00:03:56.106 --> 00:03:59.084
because I always dreamt of doing it,

00:03:59.084 --> 00:04:01.705
so, yeah, it could be the ultimate dream,

00:04:01.705 --> 00:04:04.297
but know that there's a lot of hard work

00:04:04.297 --> 00:04:05.388
that people don't see,

00:04:05.388 --> 00:04:07.555
a lot of toiling at night,

00:04:08.637 --> 00:04:10.259
a lot of sleepless nights,

00:04:10.259 --> 00:04:14.919
a lot of traveling, and some
stuff, you don't want to do,

00:04:14.919 --> 00:04:17.050
but you just do it for the love of it,

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:20.936
so if you want to do it for
fame or money, forget it.

00:04:20.936 --> 00:04:22.109
Stop now.

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:24.258
But if you want to do
it for the love of it,

00:04:24.258 --> 00:04:26.169
keep on going.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:30.262
Everyone has their own
definition of a role model.

00:04:30.262 --> 00:04:32.943
For me, I'm 21, so I'm
going to live my life

00:04:32.943 --> 00:04:34.692
like I'm a 21-year-old.

00:04:34.692 --> 00:04:36.983
I'm going to dress like I'm a 21-year-old.

00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:38.946
I know I have a five-year-old fan at home,

00:04:38.946 --> 00:04:40.923
but I can't live my life
like a five-year-old,

00:04:40.923 --> 00:04:42.246
because I'm not five,

00:04:42.246 --> 00:04:46.980
but, at 21, for a 21-year-old
to see the way I act

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.232
and see the way I dress, that's fine,

00:04:49.232 --> 00:04:51.174
and I can only be a Rihanna model,

00:04:51.174 --> 00:04:52.826
because that's who I am.

00:04:52.826 --> 00:04:55.546
I can't please everybody.

00:04:55.546 --> 00:04:56.379
It's too hard.

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.646
(laughs)

00:04:57.646 --> 00:05:00.250
- [Host] Raquel wants to know
if it's hard to remain you

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:03.667
with all the success at such a young age.

00:05:06.012 --> 00:05:09.095
- No, I would say it can be very easy

00:05:10.551 --> 00:05:12.968
to be led astray or caught up

00:05:14.577 --> 00:05:18.819
and sucked into the fame
and the bright lights

00:05:18.819 --> 00:05:20.986
and everything being grit.

00:05:23.477 --> 00:05:25.937
It can be easy to do that,

00:05:25.937 --> 00:05:28.767
but I have great people around me,

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:32.709
and a lot of people that I've
known since my childhood,

00:05:32.709 --> 00:05:35.278
a lot of people I trust, my big brothers,

00:05:35.278 --> 00:05:38.000
Jay-Z, Jay Brown, and Tata.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.049
They're my backbone, and, at this point,

00:05:40.049 --> 00:05:42.011
I'm in super good hands with them,

00:05:42.011 --> 00:05:43.544
and they keep me grounded.

00:05:43.544 --> 00:05:45.004
They keep me in check.

00:05:45.004 --> 00:05:47.404
My mother is still my mother,

00:05:47.404 --> 00:05:48.516
(laughing)

00:05:48.516 --> 00:05:51.558
and she also checks me on the reg.

00:05:51.558 --> 00:05:52.391
- [Host] Yeah?

00:05:52.391 --> 00:05:53.224
- Yeah.

00:05:53.224 --> 00:05:54.369
- [Host] On the reg.

00:05:54.369 --> 00:05:55.617
- I just had a dream.

00:05:55.617 --> 00:05:56.621
I had an idea.

00:05:56.621 --> 00:05:58.093
I knew what I wanted to do,

00:05:58.093 --> 00:05:59.634
and this is what I was going to do.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:04.240
All I wanted to do was
make music internationally.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.240
In Barbados, it's an
unrealistic goal, you know?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.196
You're a small little island
away from the United States.

00:06:13.196 --> 00:06:17.279
- What has been Jay's best advice to you?

00:06:17.279 --> 00:06:19.638
- In the beginning of my career,

00:06:19.638 --> 00:06:23.798
I remember "Pon de Replay"
started doing really well,

00:06:23.798 --> 00:06:26.675
and he came up to me at
a showcase, and he said,

00:06:26.675 --> 00:06:28.471
"You must be a really great person,

00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:31.428
because great things
keep happening for you.

00:06:31.428 --> 00:06:33.652
Don't ever change who you are.

00:06:33.652 --> 00:06:36.319
Always remain humble, the same."

00:06:37.521 --> 00:06:40.948
It kind of rings in my
ear that, every day,

00:06:40.948 --> 00:06:43.880
I hear that, and it's stuck with me.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.547
I have a lot to be grateful for.

00:06:48.614 --> 00:06:49.763
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:06:49.763 --> 00:06:52.844
I made this video because
Kristina Swagger asked me to,

00:06:52.844 --> 00:06:54.706
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want me

00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:56.866
to profile next, leave
it in the comments below,

00:06:56.866 --> 00:06:57.966
and I'll see what I can do.

00:06:57.966 --> 00:06:59.999
I'd also love to know which
of Rihanna's top 10 rules

00:06:59.999 --> 00:07:02.072
had the biggest impact on you and why.

00:07:02.072 --> 00:07:04.792
Leave it in the comments, and
I will join in the discussion.

00:07:04.792 --> 00:07:06.790
I also want to give a
quick shout-out to Tashana.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.885
Thank you so much, Tashana,
for buying my book.

00:07:08.885 --> 00:07:10.622
For those of you who want
a chance at a shout-out

00:07:10.622 --> 00:07:13.125
in a future video, make sure
to pick up a copy of the book,

00:07:13.125 --> 00:07:15.436
and then, email in your
receipt, so we can keep track.

00:07:15.436 --> 00:07:17.083
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:07:17.083 --> 00:07:19.856
Continue to believe or
whatever your one word is,

00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:21.689
and I'll see you soon.

00:07:27.359 --> 00:07:29.856
- I can't tell you where I
see myself in five years,

00:07:29.856 --> 00:07:32.189
but I can tell you that
I will work my best

00:07:32.189 --> 00:07:34.618
to be the most successful
artist that I can be

00:07:34.618 --> 00:07:36.459
in five years.

00:07:36.459 --> 00:07:38.119
- [Matt] What do you want
to be remembered for?

00:07:38.119 --> 00:07:41.432
When you're an older lady
and you're about to retire,

00:07:41.432 --> 00:07:43.642
what is the thing you
want to be remembered for?

00:07:43.642 --> 00:07:47.305
- Remembered as Rihanna,
remembered as being the artist

00:07:47.305 --> 00:07:48.936
from the Caribbean who came here

00:07:48.936 --> 00:07:51.269
and made it internationally,

00:07:52.216 --> 00:07:53.818
just remembered as me,

00:07:53.818 --> 00:07:55.583
'cause I am true to my music,

00:07:55.583 --> 00:07:57.164
and I just want people to realize that

00:07:57.164 --> 00:07:58.926
and appreciate me for that.

00:07:58.926 --> 00:08:01.977
Okay, Jim, if you could name a planet,

00:08:01.977 --> 00:08:03.178
what would it be called?

00:08:03.178 --> 00:08:04.609
- Okay, this is the
most ridiculous question

00:08:04.609 --> 00:08:05.442
I've ever heard.

00:08:05.442 --> 00:08:06.275
- I know.

00:08:06.275 --> 00:08:09.018
- But, if I could name a planet,

00:08:09.018 --> 00:08:11.435
I would call it Jim's Planet,

00:08:12.803 --> 00:08:16.504
because I don't see any
reason to mess around

00:08:16.504 --> 00:08:18.655
and be unclear with what's going on.

00:08:18.655 --> 00:08:20.585
I was allowed to name a planet,

00:08:20.585 --> 00:08:22.747
and so, I'm going to call it Jim's Planet.

00:08:22.747 --> 00:08:25.414
- I would probably name it Jhat.

00:08:26.671 --> 00:08:30.838
It's become a language of
sorts between my assistant

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.007
and I, her name is Jen,

00:08:33.007 --> 00:08:34.581
which turned into Jhat.

00:08:34.581 --> 00:08:35.991
- And how do you spell that?

00:08:35.991 --> 00:08:37.974
- J-H-A-T, that's how it is in my phone.

00:08:37.974 --> 00:08:38.807
- See?

00:08:38.807 --> 00:08:40.281
Oh, my God, I would have gone S-H-A,

00:08:40.281 --> 00:08:41.134
without a doubt.

00:08:41.134 --> 00:08:43.445
- (laughs) Everybody does that.

00:08:43.445 --> 00:08:44.278
- I like that.

00:08:44.278 --> 00:08:46.028
It has meaning, Jhat.

00:08:47.247 --> 00:08:50.996
Rihanna, on your planet,
what would the main rules be?

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:52.333
- Free shoes for everyone.

00:08:52.333 --> 00:08:53.186
- That's a good plan.

00:08:53.186 --> 00:08:57.353
- Always, any kind, and ice
cream, tons of ice cream.

00:09:00.616 --> 00:09:02.457
You can only eat ice cream.

00:09:02.457 --> 00:09:04.520
That's the only food I'm going to have.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.080
- You all going to need a good
healthcare plan on that planet,

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.159
but you will have good feet.

00:09:08.159 --> 00:09:09.590
- Tons of ice cream!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:10.930
And no diabetes.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.922
- That's not logical, now.

00:09:12.922 --> 00:09:14.220
- Oh, and no ...

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.514
Yeah, you can't ...
- Well, there's more.

00:09:15.514 --> 00:09:16.535
No what?

00:09:16.535 --> 00:09:17.598
You can't what?

00:09:17.598 --> 00:09:18.431
- You can't gain weight. (laughs)

00:09:18.431 --> 00:09:19.264
- Criticize?

00:09:19.264 --> 00:09:24.079
You can't gain weight? (laughing)

00:09:24.079 --> 00:09:26.387
I don't know about this.

00:09:26.387 --> 00:09:27.220
I don't have to move there.

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:29.342
I have my own planet.

00:09:29.342 --> 00:09:31.824
- What three things would
you take with you from earth

00:09:31.824 --> 00:09:33.023
to your planet?

00:09:33.023 --> 00:09:34.976
- I would take Todd, my partner.

00:09:34.976 --> 00:09:38.116
I would take Otis, my white dog,

00:09:38.116 --> 00:09:39.938
and I would take Rufus, my Shih Tzu.

00:09:39.938 --> 00:09:40.771
(Rihanna laughs)

00:09:40.771 --> 00:09:43.071
And the rest of you can piss off.

00:09:43.071 --> 00:09:45.053
What three things would you take?

00:09:45.053 --> 00:09:49.122
- Jhat, 'cause she can
pretty much facilitate

00:09:49.122 --> 00:09:51.329
every other thing that I need,

00:09:51.329 --> 00:09:53.496
my iPod, my iPod speakers.

00:09:55.143 --> 00:09:57.756
- What skill or talent
would you like to learn?

00:09:57.756 --> 00:09:59.188
- To whistle.

00:09:59.188 --> 00:10:00.137
- I can't either.

00:10:00.137 --> 00:10:00.970
- Really?

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:01.803
- I can't.
- You see?

00:10:01.803 --> 00:10:02.789
- I'm very surprised a musician can't.

00:10:02.789 --> 00:10:04.410
- I feel so much bet ...

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.243
What?

00:10:06.141 --> 00:10:07.333
- I'm sorry.

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:08.166
You know what?

00:10:08.166 --> 00:10:09.385
I don't even mean that,

00:10:09.385 --> 00:10:12.177
because I consider myself
my own level of musician

00:10:12.177 --> 00:10:13.010
in what I do.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:16.319
- I've been trying to learn
how to whistle for decades.

00:10:16.319 --> 00:10:17.770
- What do you think the problem is?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:18.931
- I just don't know.

00:10:18.931 --> 00:10:21.012
I think you either can or you can't.

00:10:21.012 --> 00:10:22.655
It's one of those things. (laughs)

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:23.894
- Have you tried hard?

00:10:23.894 --> 00:10:26.203
- Yes, and it sounds just like that.

00:10:26.203 --> 00:10:27.345
- So you won't even do it.

00:10:27.345 --> 00:10:28.178
- Nope.

00:10:28.178 --> 00:10:29.011
- That's probably wise.

00:10:29.011 --> 00:10:31.830
- What secret talent
could you teach the Boov?

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.584
- I get the impression they don't know ...

00:10:33.584 --> 00:10:35.437
Like, they would not know what a piano was

00:10:35.437 --> 00:10:36.459
if they saw it.

00:10:36.459 --> 00:10:37.292
Like, they'd be like,

00:10:37.292 --> 00:10:38.679
"What is this used for?"

00:10:38.679 --> 00:10:40.288
And so, I want to say I could teach them

00:10:40.288 --> 00:10:41.656
to play the piano, 'cause I do play piano.

00:10:41.656 --> 00:10:42.489
- Oh, you do?

00:10:42.489 --> 00:10:43.322
- I do.

00:10:43.322 --> 00:10:44.688
- Speaking of musicians.

00:10:44.688 --> 00:10:45.878
- I know, and I can't whistle.

00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:46.998
- Uh-huh.

00:10:46.998 --> 00:10:49.279
- I took it back as soon as I said it.

00:10:49.279 --> 00:10:50.469
I was just surprised!

00:10:50.469 --> 00:10:51.500
I always felt like ...

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.462
Do you know how often a
script calls for an actor

00:10:53.462 --> 00:10:54.578
to whistle?
(Rihanna laughs)

00:10:54.578 --> 00:10:55.681
It's frequent.

00:10:55.681 --> 00:10:57.122
- That is really good to know.

00:10:57.122 --> 00:10:58.632
I would have never guess that.

00:10:58.632 --> 00:10:59.465
- That I played?

00:10:59.465 --> 00:11:00.298
- Yeah.

00:11:00.298 --> 00:11:01.174
- 'Cause you don't think
I have an ounce of rhythm?

00:11:01.174 --> 00:11:02.683
What?

00:11:02.683 --> 00:11:03.656
What's the judgment you've made?

00:11:03.656 --> 00:11:04.756
- That is really mean.

00:11:04.756 --> 00:11:06.799
- No. No!
- That's not what I said.

00:11:06.799 --> 00:11:08.128
- No, you're right.

00:11:08.128 --> 00:11:09.510
I put words in your mouth. But ...

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:12.261
- But you're so great at acting.

00:11:12.261 --> 00:11:13.475
- Yeah? That ...

00:11:13.475 --> 00:11:15.433
- That I couldn't picture
you having any room

00:11:15.433 --> 00:11:16.903
for another skill.
- Having time for anything ...

00:11:16.903 --> 00:11:17.904
Absolutely. Absolutely.

00:11:17.904 --> 00:11:18.737
Thank you.

00:11:18.737 --> 00:11:20.046
- See how I changed that?

00:11:20.046 --> 00:11:21.455
- That's really sweet.
- See what I did? (laughs)

